This is the third of five introductory messages about comp.sources.games.
The first described how to submit sources to comp.sources.games, where
the archive sites are, and how to contact them.  The second posting is
a list of sources posted to this newsgroup arranged by volume/issue
number.  The fourth posting is an index of the patches that have been
posted in c.s.g. The fifth posting is an index of sources in the games
archive on saab.  This posting lists the sources that have been
published in this newsgroup. It provides a listing of the Archive-name,
the Volume/Issue and the Subject for each posting.

Note: in the uunet archives all archive names are converted to lower
case, thus NetHack3/Patch7c becomes nethack3/patch7c; GB2/Part01
becomes gb2/part01, etc. This is because of a limitation in their uucp
retrieval software and probably doesn't apply to other archive sites.

